# The webapp Dockerfile installs dependencies, then copies the source over the
# top. Without this, a developer's host node_modules -- a pnpm symlink farm
# pointing at paths that do not exist in the image -- lands on top of the clean
# install and every import fails to resolve (TS2307 on @wso2/oxygen-ui and
# anything else). It also keeps ~530MB out of the build context.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs and test artefacts: rebuilt in the image, never copied in.
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.turbo
**/.vite

# Local environment files never belong in an image.
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
